  "worked_solution": "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
